---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import { SITE } from "../lib/site";

const updated = "October 10, 2026";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy Policy"
  description="How Leverage AI collects, uses, and protects information submitted through this website."
  canonicalPath="/privacy"
>
  <section class="section">
    <article class="shell surface stack prose legal-page">
      <p class="eyebrow">Last updated {updated}</p>
      <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
      <p>
        This policy explains what information Leverage AI LLC collects through this website, why we
        use it, and the choices available to you. It applies to leverageai.network and does not
        govern the independent websites shown in case-study embeds.
      </p>

      <h2>Information you provide</h2>
      <p>
        When you use the contact form or email us, you may provide your name, email address, phone
        number, service interest, business information, and the details included in your message.
        Please do not send sensitive personal, financial, health, or account-access information
        through the form.
      </p>

      <h2>Information collected automatically</h2>
      <p>
        The website host and security infrastructure may process standard technical information
        such as IP address, browser type, requested pages, timestamps, and security events. This
        information is used to deliver the site, diagnose errors, prevent abuse, and maintain
        security.
      </p>
      <p>
        This site does not use advertising pixels, does not use session recording, and does not
        sell personal information.
      </p>

      <h2>Analytics</h2>
      <p>
        We use privacy-focused analytics to understand which pages are useful and how the site
        performs, so we can improve it. We use two services:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>PostHog</strong> records page views, clicks on links and buttons, and page-speed
          measurements. It runs in a cookieless mode: it does not set cookies or store identifiers in
          your browser, and it does not build a profile of you. To count visits without cookies,
          PostHog computes a one-way hash from your IP address, browser user agent, our site
          name and a random value that changes every day and is then deleted, so visits cannot be
          linked across days or tied back to you. It never records what you type into forms.
          Requests pass through our own server before reaching PostHog.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Cloudflare Web Analytics</strong>, provided by our hosting and security provider,
          measures page views and page performance without cookies.
        </li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        These services act on our behalf, and we use their data only to operate and improve this
        website.
      </p>

      <h2>Cookies</h2>
      <p>
        This site does not set cookies for analytics, advertising or tracking, so there is no
        cookie banner. If that changes, we will ask for your consent first and update this page.
      </p>

      <h2>Do Not Track and Global Privacy Control</h2>
      <p>
        If your browser sends a Global Privacy Control or Do Not Track signal, PostHog analytics does
        not load at all during your visit. Basic technical processing needed to deliver and secure
        the site, described above, still applies.
      </p>

      <h2>Embedded third-party websites</h2>
      <p>
        Case-study pages may display live previews from daleyorganics.com or
        oregonsmbdirectory.com. Loading those previews may allow the third-party website and its
        hosting providers to receive technical request data. Their own privacy practices apply to
        those interactions.
      </p>

      <h2>How information is used</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Respond to inquiries and discuss requested services.</li>
        <li>Evaluate whether Leverage AI is a good fit for the problem described.</li>
        <li>Operate, secure, troubleshoot, and improve the website and contact workflow.</li>
        <li>Maintain business records and comply with legal obligations.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Sharing and retention</h2>
      <p>
        Information may be processed by service providers that support website hosting, email,
        security, analytics, and lead delivery. Leverage AI does not sell personal information. Inquiry
        information is retained only as long as reasonably needed for communication, business
        records, security, or legal obligations.
      </p>

      <h2>Your choices and privacy requests</h2>
      <p>
        You may ask what personal information we hold about you or request correction or deletion
        by emailing <a href={`mailto:${SITE.email}`}>{SITE.email}</a>. We may need to verify the
        request and may retain information when required for security, recordkeeping, or legal
        reasons.
      </p>
      <p>
        Oregon privacy rights depend on whether a business meets the Oregon Consumer Privacy Act's
        coverage thresholds. Leverage AI will evaluate valid requests under applicable law even
        when a particular statutory requirement does not apply.
      </p>

      <h2>Children</h2>
      <p>
        This website is intended for businesses and is not directed to children under 13. Do not
        submit information about a child through the contact form.
      </p>

      <h2>Changes</h2>
      <p>
        Material changes will be reflected on this page with a new “last updated” date.
      </p>

      <h2>Contact</h2>
      <p>
        Leverage AI LLC · {SITE.location} ·
        <a href={`mailto:${SITE.email}`}>{SITE.email}</a>
      </p>

      <h2>Official resources</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><a href="https://www.doj.state.or.us/consumer-protection/id-theft-data-breaches/privacy/">Oregon Department of Justice: Consumer Privacy</a></li>
        <li><a href="https://www.ftc.gov/business-guidance/privacy-security">Federal Trade Commission: Privacy and Security</a></li>
      </ul>
    </article>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
